---
description: Branch, commit, and deploy policy for this project
alwaysApply: true
---

# Nothing reaches `main` without being asked

The user decides when work ships. Do not `git commit` to `main`, `git push`,
or merge unless the user asks for it in that message. Silence is not consent,
and neither is "the change is finished".

Note: this repo's default checkout is `main` itself, so an absent-minded
`git commit` lands on `main` directly. When work needs committing, create a
branch first and say so.

# Verify on localhost before proposing to ship

The user runs `npm run dev` on port 3000. Confirm the change works there
before calling it done — the dev server hot-reloads, so edits are visible
immediately.

Before handing work back, check:

- `npm run build` succeeds
- `npm run lint` is clean
- flows adjacent to the change still work, especially auth (`/login`,
  `/signup`), `/profile/me`, `/events`, and anything reading `profiles`

# Package manager

`ai-behavior.mdc` says pnpm, but the lockfile and the user's terminal use
`npm`. Use `npm` for scripts in this repo.
